beyondthestars.gui.kerr.panel.modules.title=Modules
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.panel.modules.footer=Run each module from its own controller.
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.run=§eRUN §7Everything is in the GUI.
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.run1=§71. Put a Black Hole Seed in a bolt bus and press Open: the hole opens at 8 SM (solar masses).
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.run2=§72. It bleeds mass as Hawking radiation, 3.2 / M² SM a tick. Small holes die fast.
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.run3=§73. The governor fires bolts from the bolt buses to hold your setpoint (2-64 SM at T1).
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.run4=§74. While open, the hole draws 8,388,608 EU/t (1 A UEV) of containment. Without power the governor stops; below 2 SM the hole evaporates. The power switch does not stop the hole.
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.run5=§75. A Black Hole Collapser in a bolt bus closes it safely: press Collapse twice.
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.bolts=§eBOLTS §7Neutronium 1/64 SM, Cosmic Neutronium 1/32, Infinity 1/16, Transcendent Metal 1/8, SpaceTime 1/4 SM a bolt; at most 4 / 8 / 16 bolts a tick with Mk I / II / III rails. The lowest rail sets the rate.
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.t2=§eT2 §7Right-click the controller with the Kerr Density Upgrade (consumed, permanent, survives a wrench): setpoints up to 512 SM, and Kerr Densification on the Compressor Module with a hole of at least 128 SM. The cage then needs the T2 reinforcement (hologram stack 2).
beyondthestars.gui.kerr.info.auto=§eAUTO §7Tick Auto in the Hole control panel: a Seed in a bolt bus then opens a closed hole, and a Collapser closes an open one, with no button. BHC Utility Hatches on the cage give redstone while the hole is open.
