beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.open=§eOPEN §7A Quasar Seed in the controller slot, then Open in Disc control: the hole starts at 64 SM with no spin, and the jets are faint for the first hour while it spins up. Collapse makes it dormant (mass kept); a Black Hole Seed re-opens it. Nothing ever destroys the hole or a block.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.feed=§eFEED §7Helium (or Hydrogen, Raw Star Matter) into the 24 rim Input Hatches; the quasar keeps 60 s of Disc (+ Hold-up with a lattice) in its own Accretion Buffer, refilled every tick. f is the share of the Eddington feed drawn: 0.85 sits Stable unattended, 1.0 rides the limit with trims for about 1.5x the output.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.disc=§eE §7The Eddington balance, target 0, on the Eye's zones: Resonant ±10 (Y 1.25), Stable ±40, Strained ±70, Critical ±100, then Breach: a blow-out. The disc re-forms over 5 min at f 0.3 or more; the hole is never lost.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.trims=§eTRIMS §7Plain Input Hatches in the 4 wall-tank sockets: the feed gas (1,000 x M/64 L a unit) raises E by 2, Spatially Enlarged Fluid (100 x M/64 L) lowers it by 2; at most 10 units a second each.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.flux=§eFLUX §7Charges b λ / 2.4 a second; at 100 the disc erupts (3x the stream for 3 s). A purge (from 20) dumps it early: the button, or a rising edge on a Burst Control Hatch in Purge mode.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.coils=§eCOILS §7Disc Field Coils T1-T4 cap the field b and the mass (256 / 1,024 / 2,048 / 4,096 SM). Coil power 2 A UXV x b² from the control box; short power: b = 0, the jets stop.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.jets=§eJETS §7G0 = λ a² b² (M/64)² Bu/t, half on each port. A crown docked on a port turns 1 Bu/t into 10^13 EU/t; a Wormhole Mouth carries it into the Conduit. A port with nothing docked vents.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.burst=§eBURST CONTROL §7A Burst Control Hatch on a cap rim reads redstone: Purge mode purges on a rising edge, Field b mode sets b = 0.5 + (tier - 0.5) x s/15. The standard rig: Directive Hatch (Disc set) bit 3 AND NOT the Eye's Transition bit 4 into it.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.auto=§eAUTOMATE §7A Stellar Field Sensor Hatch reads E, flux, λ, a, M, Bu/t and more; a Directive Hatch's Disc set gives the trims and the purge as bits. OpenComputers: bts_quasar. Keep the quasar chunk-loaded: an unloaded chunk freezes it and pauses every machine it feeds.
