beyondthestars.gui.quasar.panel.hint.lattice=Put more gas in than f draws: it holds the mass over the safe limit, then grows the hole (up to 5x the Eddington feed).
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.panel.hint.nolattice=Build the Supermassive Lattice round the quasar and reach Saturation (4,096 SM Stable for 1 hour on MagMatter coils).
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.eu=§eEU/t §71 Bu/t = 10^13 EU/t once a crown turns it into power. A maxed 4,096 SM quasar's 9,796 Bu/t is 9.8e16 EU/t, 98 quadrillion (quadrillion = 10^15, quintillion = 10^18). Every Bu/t in this GUI shows its EU/t beside it.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.lattice=§eSUPERMASSIVE LATTICE §7An armillary cage round this quasar, its last upgrade (in place: the same hole). It counts after Saturation (4,096 SM Stable for 1 hour on MagMatter coils). Safe limit / top: L1 Superdense Ergomatter 16,384 / 65,536 SM, L2 White Hole Matter 65,536 / 262,144, L3 Universium 262,144 / 4,194,304, L4 Constrained Eternity 4,194,304 / 67,108,864.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.intake=§eINTAKE §7All the gas drawn in a second, up to 5x the Eddington feed: Disc (f, the only part that moves E), then Hold-up (3x x Eddington; holds the mass over the safe limit; short, the extra leaks back, halving each hour), then Growth (the rest). Power past 4,096 SM grows as the square root of mass: x2 (2.0e17 EU/t) at 16,384 SM, up to x31 (3.0e18 EU/t) at the L4 top.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.overdrive=§eOVERDRIVE §7L3 or better: output toward x100 (9.8e18 EU/t, about 10 quintillion) for 100,000 x o² L/s each of Molten MHDCSM and Molten Universium. Half Overdrive gives about 90 % of the gain. Running dry fades it over 1 s; nothing breaks.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.unbound=§eUNBOUND §7L4 and Unbind: the setpoint may pass 67,108,864 SM. Each doubling n halves the Overdrive upkeep, for a Primordial Matter anchor of 1,024 x 4^(n²) L/s (4,096 L/s at n 1). A short anchor sheds safely to what the supply pays for; nothing is ever destroyed.
beyondthestars.gui.quasar.info.horizon=§eAUTOMATE THE LATTICE §7Directive Horizon set: [1] hold-up short [2] buffer under 30 s [4] anchor short [8] Overdrive upkeep short. Burst Control Hatch modes: Hold (the setpoint, safe limit 0 .. top 15), Overdrive (o = s/15), Shed (a rising edge). Sensor channels for every number here. OpenComputers bts_quasar: getBand, getIntake, getHoldUp, getBuffer, getOverdrive, getAnchor, getHorizon, setMassSetpoint, setOverdrive, setUnbound, shed.
