beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.mouth=§eWORMHOLE §7Two mouths are one wormhole: a stream entering one ring through its front face leaves the partner out of its back, at any distance, even in another dimension. Pair them with a Data Stick. On a quasar's jet port: the ring's front-face centre on the port cell, facing the quasar.
beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.mirror=§eMIRROR §7Turns a stream through 90 degrees: in through the front throat, out of the side one (or the other way round). Its facing picks the plane.
beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.junction=§eJUNCTION §7Split: the big throat in; out 3 takes its fixed share first, out 1 and out 2 share the rest by c + k x (s/15 - 0.5), s from its Burst Control Hatch. Combine: three in, the sum out of the big throat.
beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.throats=§eTHROATS §7A Conduit Throat in the controller: Mk I / II / III / IV carry 24 / 384 / 6,144 / 524,288 Bu/t (2.4e14 / 3.8e15 / 6.1e16 / 5.2e18 EU/t) through the whole element; the excess is clipped, never damage.
beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.upkeep=§eUPKEEP §7One unit an element: Molten SpaceTime 4 / 16 / 64 L/s, or Ergomatter 0.25 / 1 / 4 L/s after Eye T7 (the fuel button: Auto / SpaceTime / Ergomatter). Short upkeep closes it; it reopens after 10 s of full upkeep.
beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.rays=§eRAYS §7A stream leaves a throat in a straight line and must reach the next throat or a GRB Receptor Port through up to 64 blocks of air. The Out rows name the target, or where it is blocked.
beyondthestars.gui.conduit.info.auto=§eAUTOMATE §7OpenComputers: bts_mouth, bts_mirror, bts_junction (getLink, getThroat, getUpkeep, isOpen; the Junction's split). Keep every element chunk-loaded.
